	(text_box "The tree stands in the base's socket (J101, a right-angle\nheader: its pins point down) and carries the perch on its\ntop (J102, the same part pointing up). Both joints follow\ngen/connectors.py. The levitation coil's current (LEV_A,\nLEV_B, 3.3 A at most) and the Hall sensor's line pass\nstraight up the trunk; the tree has its own LP5036 (U101,\nI2C 0x32) for the owls' eyes, the stars, the wisps and the\nperch's two downlights." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.7800 200.6600 0) (size 50.8000 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bf8368a0-2b6c-34bd-a5b7-8a918521f965"))
	(text_box "Owls A, B, C: an orange eye pair each, one bank\neach (OUT0-1, 3-4, 6-7), so each owl's eyes open\ntogether. Stars OUT9-14 (violet), wisps OUT18-21\n(purple). R on IREF: 22 mA at most per output." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 160.0200 200.6600 0) (size 46.9900 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
